### api/projects -- reading projects (M4 PR a)
#
# Needs an Auth0 access token for the /me routes (see me.http). Put a project id in
# .env as `projectId=…` and a user id as `userId=…`.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}
@accessToken = {{$dotenv accessToken}}
@projectId = {{$dotenv projectId}}
@userId = {{$dotenv userId}}

###
# @name getProject
# 200 a public, published project, no token needed. A token, when sent, identifies the
# owner, who also reads private and draft projects. Anyone else gets 404, the same
# body as an unknown id. A bad token is 401, never anonymous.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{projectId}}

###
# @name getProjectAsOwner
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name listMyProjects
# 200 { items, nextCursor }: the caller's projects in every state. Filters: state
# (published|private|draft), category, status, tag, technology, q. Sort: newest
# (default), oldest, updated, name_asc, name_desc. Pass nextCursor back as cursor with
# the same sort; a cursor for another sort, an unknown key, or limit over the maximum is 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/projects?sort=name_asc&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name listMyDrafts
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/projects?state=draft&q=garden
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name listUserProjects
# 200 the user's public, published projects, no token needed. 404 when the user's profile
# is private (and the caller is not its owner) or the user does not exist.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/users/{{userId}}/projects?category=research&technology=python

###
# @name nextPage
# nextCursor from the previous response
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/projects?limit=10&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
